{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8RMnB7iqHkfrP4cGAjK3v","type":"tool_result","content":"# slugify\n\nImplement `slugify(text, max_length=None)` in `src/slugify.py`.\n\n1. Normalize `text` with `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", ...)` and drop every non-ASCII character.\n2. Lowercase it.\n3. Replace each run of characters that are not `a-z` or `0-9` with a single `-`.\n4. Strip leading and trailing `-`.\n5. If `max_length` is given and the slug is longer than `max_length`:\n   - cut it to the first `max_length` characters;\n   - if the cut split a word (the character just before the cut and the character just\n     after it are both alphanumeric), drop that partial word;\n   - strip trailing `-`;\n   - if this leaves an empty string, return the first `max_length` characters of the\n     slug instead, with trailing `-` stripped.\n6. If nothing is left, return `\"\"`.\n\n## Running the tests\n\n    python3 -m pytest -q\n---\n./src/slugify.py\n./pytest.ini\n./README.md\n./tests/test_slugify.py\n---\n\"\"\"URL slug generation. See README.md for the specification.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef slugify(text, max_length=None):\n    raise NotImplementedError\n---\nfrom slugify import slugify\n\n\ndef test_basic():\n    assert slugify(\"Hello World\") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_accents_and_punctuation():\n    assert slugify(\"  Héllo,  Wörld!! \") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_symbols():\n    assert slugify(\"C++ & Python 3.12\") == \"c-python-3-12\"\n\n\ndef test_only_separators():\n    assert slugify(\"---\") == \"\"\n    assert slugify(\"\") == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_non_ascii_dropped():\n    assert slugify(\"日本語 text\") == \"text\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_not_needed():\n    assert slugify(\"naïve café\", max_length=20) == \"naive-cafe\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_drops_partial_word():\n    assert slugify(\"the quick brown fox\", max_length=12) == \"the-quick\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_on_boundary():\n    assert slugify(\"the quick brown fox\", max_length=9) == \"the-quick\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_single_long_word():\n    assert slugify(\"supercalifragilistic\", max_length=5) == \"super\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d41edcf-958b-4ab2-8ffa-7d96ab07cb05","uuid":"833f36f8-5673-47e3-8b32-a60dc3eaa447","timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:22:57.611Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# slugify\n\nImplement `slugify(text, max_length=None)` in `src/slugify.py`.\n\n1. Normalize `text` with `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", ...)` and drop every non-ASCII character.\n2. Lowercase it.\n3. Replace each run of characters that are not `a-z` or `0-9` with a single `-`.\n4. Strip leading and trailing `-`.\n5. If `max_length` is given and the slug is longer than `max_length`:\n   - cut it to the first `max_length` characters;\n   - if the cut split a word (the character just before the cut and the character just\n     after it are both alphanumeric), drop that partial word;\n   - strip trailing `-`;\n   - if this leaves an empty string, return the first `max_length` characters of the\n     slug instead, with trailing `-` stripped.\n6. If nothing is left, return `\"\"`.\n\n## Running the tests\n\n    python3 -m pytest -q\n---\n./src/slugify.py\n./pytest.ini\n./README.md\n./tests/test_slugify.py\n---\n\"\"\"URL slug generation. See README.md for the specification.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef slugify(text, max_length=None):\n    raise NotImplementedError\n---\nfrom slugify import slugify\n\n\ndef test_basic():\n    assert slugify(\"Hello World\") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_accents_and_punctuation():\n    assert slugify(\"  Héllo,  Wörld!! \") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_symbols():\n    assert slugify(\"C++ & Python 3.12\") == \"c-python-3-12\"\n\n\ndef test_only_separators():\n    assert slugify(\"---\") == \"\"\n    assert slugify(\"\") == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_non_ascii_dropped():\n    assert slugify(\"日本語 text\") == \"text\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_not_needed():\n    assert slugify(\"naïve café\", max_length=20) == \"naive-cafe\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_drops_partial_word():\n    assert slugify(\"the quick brown fox\", max_length=12) == \"the-quick\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_on_boundary():\n    assert slugify(\"the quick brown fox\", max_length=9) == \"the-quick\"\n\n\ndef test_max_length_single_long_word():\n    assert slugify(\"supercalifragilistic\", max_length=5) == \"super\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K8RMnB7iqHkfrP4cGAjK3v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
